5533a235","github_link":"https://github.com/MatterHackers/agg-sharp/commit/edda4e1cfe2d7615789b546857507c415533a235","commit_subject":"PlanarRegionSimplifier merges each coplanar region of a mesh and retriangulates it with Manifold's ear clipper, keeping every vertex a non-planar neighbour shares so the mesh stays watertight: a distance-field Dilate of a block drops from 89k to 5k triangles and an L bracket from 73k to 722, with volume unchanged to 1e-6 and removed vertices within 7e-7 of the new surface; a region that would pinch, mis-tile or go non-manifold keeps its original faces","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"MatterHackers/agg-sharp","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-01T14:48:21Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"c870a9c3860f182a7fbc045e595fe6b3eaed1b5d","github_link":"https://github.com/MatterHackers/agg-sharp/commit/c870a9c3860f182a7fbc045e595fe6b3eaed1b5d","commit_subject":"GridMarchingCubes resolves ambiguous faces with the asymptotic decider, so a feature thinner than a cell stays joined: an eroded gear's tooth tips no longer split off as one-cell islands (exact keeps them attached, and now so does the distance-field result). Cells with an ambiguous face are built from per-face segments chained into loops; the face decision is deterministic and symmetric between the two cells that share it, so the mesh stays closed and manifold, which a seeded fuzz of 300 random fields (integer ties included) pins","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"datacenter/ACI-Pre-Upgrade-Validation-Script","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-01T14:48:10Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"d2815bf23ea91e63cba86e9efb2d1ede491d300e","github_link":"https://github.com/datacenter/ACI-Pre-Upgrade-Validation-Script/commit/d2815bf23ea91e63cba86e9efb2d1ede491d300e","commit_subject":"Merge pull request #470 from datacenter/codex/integration-check-workflow","ai_tool":"Codex"},{"repo_name":"expertanalytics/rasputin","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-01T14:47:52Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"3c32d3d1d4aa62033aee5206